Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:06:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 66/71] Trigger auto-compaction at 70k instead of 80k

`ModelInfo::auto_compact_token_limit()` is `min(config_limit, context_window *
9/10)`, so the catalog entry is what binds: 180,000 is never the smaller number.

Compaction now leaves a 6k verbatim assistant tail on top of the user messages,
the regenerated initial context and the summary, which puts the post-compaction
floor near 10k rather than the ~3.4k upstream's version left. Triggering at 70k
holds the peak prompt down while still leaving about 60k of runway per window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/models-manager/models.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
index f650abd332..227d379eff 100644
--- a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
+++ b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
       "model_specialty": null,
       "context_window": 200000,
       "max_context_window": 200000,
-      "auto_compact_token_limit": 80000,
+      "auto_compact_token_limit": 70000,
       "comp_hash": "2911",
       "default_reasoning_summary": "none",
       "display_name": "GLM 5.3",
